    bib_breath_coherent_why:"稳定节律(HRV)——具有稳定和扎根的作用。",
    bib_breath_long_exhale_title:"延长呼气",
    bib_breath_long_exhale_tag:"行为疗法",
    bib_breath_long_exhale_why:"长呼气传递安全信号——减少压力和紧张。",
    bib_breath_phys_sigh_title:"生理叹息",
    bib_breath_phys_sigh_tag:"Stanford / Huberman",
    bib_breath_phys_sigh_why:"极速平静——适合急性压力(无需屏气)。",
    bib_breath_nostril_title:"交替鼻孔",
    bib_breath_nostril_tag:"Nadi Shodhana",
    bib_breath_nostril_why:"平静稳定的交替——可支持专注力和内在平衡。",
    bib_breath_pursed_title:"缩唇呼吸",
    bib_breath_pursed_tag:"肺科学",
    bib_breath_pursed_why:"减缓呼吸流速——帮助放慢节奏。",
    bib_breath_counting_title:"呼吸计数",
    bib_breath_counting_tag:"正念疗法",
    bib_breath_counting_why:"将注意力从思维循环中抽离——带来结构感。",
    bib_breath_observe_title:"呼吸观察",
    bib_breath_observe_tag:"MBSR (Kabat-Zinn)",
    bib_breath_observe_why:"不强求——只是观察。当你过度用力时特别有效。",
    bib_prog_sleep_title:"晚间仪式",
    bib_prog_sleep_tag:"晚间例行 · 每日 · 60秒",
    bib_prog_sleep_why:"当大脑无法关闭时的理想选择。简短、平静、可重复——直到成为习惯。",
    bib_prog_workday_title:"工作日重置",
    bib_prog_workday_tag:"会议间隙 · 60秒",
    bib_prog_workday_why:"适用于充满会议、压力和缺少喘息空间的日子。60秒往往就够了。",
    bib_prog_morning_title:"晨间仪式",
    bib_prog_morning_tag:"早晨 · 5天 · 60秒",
    bib_prog_morning_why:"在解锁第一台设备前，以清晰的头脑开始一天。",
    bib_prog_emotion_title:"保持情绪稳定",
    bib_prog_emotion_tag:"课程 · 3天 · 情绪",
    bib_prog_emotion_why:"当情绪高涨时——这个课程帮你学会回应而非反应。",
    bib_prog_focus_title:"专注周",
    bib_prog_focus_tag:"课程 · 5天 · 深度工作",
    bib_prog_focus_why:"无需意志力就能获得更敏锐的专注力。每日60秒，带来不同。",
    bib_know_stressloop_title:"压力是个循环",
    bib_know_stressloop_tag:"知识 · 日常生活",
    bib_know_stressloop_body:"压力常常感觉像'脑中负荷过重'——但其实是身体状态。当你短暂下调(呼吸、肌肉张力、注意力)时，思维会自动变得更清晰。",
    bib_know_panic_title:"急性：不知所措时该怎么办",
    bib_know_panic_tag:"知识 · 紧急援助",
    bib_know_panic_body:"当情况变得急性时，避免长时间屏气。选择平静的延长呼气。目标不是完美，而是发出小小的'我很安全'信号。之后再反思。",
    bib_know_habit_title:"微习惯胜过自律",
    bib_know_habit_tag:"知识 · 动机",
    bib_know_vagus_title:"迷走神经与你",
    bib_know_vagus_tag:"知识 · 神经系统",
    bib_know_vagus_body:"The vagus nerve connects brain and gut – it's the information highway of the parasympathetic system. Slow exhaling, humming, or cold water on your face stimulate it directly. That's why breathing exercises work so fast.",
    bib_know_cortisol_title:"Understanding cortisol",
    bib_know_cortisol_tag:"Knowledge · Stress hormones",
    bib_know_cortisol_body:"Cortisol isn't the enemy – it keeps you going. It becomes problematic when levels stay elevated long-term. Regular mini-breaks lower the baseline level over weeks. That's measurable.",
    bib_know_breathscience_title:"The science of breathing",
    bib_know_breathscience_tag:"Knowledge · Research",
    bib_know_breathscience_body:"Studies show: just 5 slow breaths increase heart rate variability (HRV). Extended exhale (4 in, 6 out) directly activates the vagus nerve and lowers heart rate within seconds.",
    bib_know_sleep_title:"Why you can't fall asleep",
    bib_know_sleep_tag:"Knowledge · Sleep",
    bib_know_sleep_body:"The brain needs a 'safety signal' to fall asleep. Thoughts and screen light block this signal. A short breathing exercise deliberately sends: 'It's calm now.' – the brain follows.",
    bib_know_hrv_title:"HRV – your stress gauge",
    bib_know_hrv_tag:"Knowledge · Measurement",
    bib_know_hrv_body:"Heart rate variability (HRV) shows how flexibly your nervous system responds to stimuli. A high value means: you're recovered and resilient. Regular breathing increases HRV – measurable after a few weeks.",
    bib_free_sub:"View free · Upgrade for access",
